# Python / Django (server/) — no .gitignore covered this codebase at all
# before now. The .gitignore files elsewhere in this repo are all
# Flutter-generated and don't touch server/.

# Local/live databases — see copilot/settings.py's DATABASES comment and
# infra/docker-compose.prod.yml: these should never be committed. A
# tracked db.sqlite3 is what caused a `git pull` on the VM to silently
# overwrite the live production database out from under a running
# container (2026-08-12). The Docker setup now keeps the real db in a
# separate volume regardless, but this stops it from being tracked in the
# first place too.
server/db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3

# Secrets — GROQ_API_KEY, HF_TOKEN, etc. live in these. Never commit them;
# server/.env.example and server/.env.production.example (tracked,
# intentionally) are the templates to copy from instead.
server/.env
server/.env.production
server/.env.*.local

# Python
server/__pycache__/
server/**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
server/*.egg-info/
server/.venv/
server/venv/

# HF model cache, if ever downloaded outside the Docker volume
server/.cache/

# admin-ui/ (Next.js control room, added 2026-08-30) — same reasoning as
# never committing server/.venv above: dependency and build output
# directories are large, regenerated by `npm install`/`npm run build`,
# and machine-specific. Committing node_modules in particular is exactly
# the kind of thing that made the old CI/CD pipeline's git-based deploy
# slow/unreliable (see the conversation history around switching to a
# proper `npm install` step on the VM instead of syncing this folder).
admin-ui/node_modules/
admin-ui/.next/
admin-ui/out/
admin-ui/.env.local